# The one ONNX Runtime the embedder crate loads (feature 449 T138, the round arbiter's `ask:449-phase4-slices` Q11; `rust/embed/`):
# Microsoft's own Linux x64 release of the version the Python's `onnxruntime` wheel was (1.31.1, the version `fastembed` ran BGE-M3 on),
# so the Rust embeds the stored index's passages and a question with the same runtime - its vectors bit for bit the Python's on the
# probes (observed 2026-11-16, method: 24 English, Japanese, Chinese and archive texts, batched and alone, both sides compared).
# `install-onnxruntime.sh` downloads and checks it, and the crate finds the library by this version. A new version: change both lines
# together (the SHA-256 is the archive's, `sha256sum onnxruntime-linux-x64-<version>.tgz`).
ONNXRUNTIME_VERSION=1.31.1
ONNXRUNTIME_SHA256=c849e36a1ef3e22d4ff217b9d1ce4a3cf5b9467b975610913ae959ad5b16bdc9
# THE FALLBACK (2026-11-28: github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime answered 404 - the repository page, its API and every release
# asset - so a fresh container could not install the archive above): PyPI's CPython 3.12 manylinux wheel of the same version, the
# build the Python's `onnxruntime` itself was, its `onnxruntime/capi/libonnxruntime.so.<version>` extracted to the same path. Its
# URL and SHA-256 are PyPI's own (`https://pypi.org/pypi/onnxruntime/1.31.1/json`); change them with the version.
ONNXRUNTIME_WHEEL_URL=https://files.pythonhosted.org/packages/eb/27/c6a823bac55b2977bea2027c3ec9393a2c1002cb9a09eb40354563e02730/onnxruntime-1.31.1-cp312-cp312-manylinux_2_28_x86_64.whl
ONNXRUNTIME_WHEEL_SHA256=1f3dea47f2f0e5117c2404cea7d21fd253ae7836a3bf167a501cdfbb2600d536
